      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`humming_is_layer_skipped` stops at a missing/empty alias and continues past a populated one. As a result, an exclusion supplied through any one of `ignored_layers`, `ignore`, or `modules_to_not_convert` is lost. `prepare_humming_moe_layer` can then select FP8 input schemas for an excluded layer.\n\n## Modifications\n\nUse the first **present** alias, matching `HummingConfig.is_layer_skipped` / `get_from_keys_or`. Explicit empty or null values keep their existing precedence over later aliases; this does not merge the lists.\n\nExtend the registered CPU schema tests to cover all three aliases, precedence, empty/null values, absent configuration, `lm_head` and dynamic exclusions, and the actual MoE input-schema selection for both `w13` and `w2`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe original 8 tests pass on the baseline. The added regressions reproduce 9 failing subcases before the fix; the complete file passes all 14 test methods after it:\n\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=999 PYTHONPATH=\"$PWD/python\" python test/registered/unit/layers/quantization/test_humming_w4afp8_schemas.py\n```\n\nTested on WSL Linux, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130, with CUDA hidden. The integration regression calls the production helper and MoE preparation with real Humming input schemas; downstream weight conversion/transforms are mocked. It covers the non-DeepEP schema path, not the separate FP8 DeepEP override. No GPU kernel or full-model accuracy claim.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this fixes configuration handling. No performance claim.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed-file pre-commit hooks pass.\n- [x] Registered CPU regression tests added and run.\n- [x] Existing alias precedence and exclusion behavior covered.\n- [x] `git diff --check` passes.\n- Documentation: no new configuration option.\n\nAI assistance was used to develop and validate this change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35515362579](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35515362579)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35515362438](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35515362438)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35515362546](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35515362546)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
